I tried e-mailing this, but it didn't work.  Here goes:

In article <2i6b1c$21v@wsintt01.info.win.tue.nl>, you write:
>In the sources (file: include/artilist.h), the entry for the Platinum
>Yendorian Express Card is as follows:
>
>A("The Platinum Yendorian Express Card", CREDIT_CARD,
>       (SPFX_NOGEN|SPFX_RESTR|SPFX_INTEL|SPFX_DEFN),
>               (SPFX_ESP|SPFX_HSPDAM), 0,
>       NO_ATTK,        NO_DFNS,        CARY(AD_MAGM),
>       CHARGE_OBJ,     A_NEUTRAL,      'T' ),
>
>Now in the second line it says SPFX_DEFN, which indicates a special
>defense granted to the player by carrying it. In the fourth line,
>however, it says NO_DFNS where the type of special defense should have
>been mentioned.
>
>My question: does the PYEC have a special defense, and if so, what is
>it?

I think the defn field (here set to NO_DFNS) only applies for weapons.
I believe the cary field (here set to CARY(AC_MAGM)) is what is used
for non-weapons.  It applies whenever you are carrying the PYEC.
MAGM is protection against magic attack.
